# PHASE 18 — STUDENT LIFECYCLE, DIGITAL DOCUMENTS, CERTIFICATES & TRANSFER CERTIFICATE MANAGEMENT

## IMPORTANT CONTEXT

This is PHASE 18 of an already-developed, production-oriented, multi-school School ERP.

DO NOT create a new application.

DO NOT rebuild the ERP from scratch.

DO NOT create a second student management system.

DO NOT duplicate existing Student, Parent, Admission, Fee, Communication, Portal, Authentication, School, Academic Session, or Reporting modules.

You must first inspect the existing codebase, database schema, APIs, authentication system, RBAC system, student module, parent module, admission module, fees module, communication module, portal, file/document handling, reporting system, audit system, and mobile/PWA implementation.

Then extend the existing architecture safely.

The ERP already contains modules from previous phases including:

- Authentication & RBAC
- Multi-school management
- Academic sessions
- Student & Parent Management
- Admissions
- Teacher & Staff Management
- Attendance
- Fees & Accounts
- Examination & Results
- Timetable & Homework
- Transport
- Library
- Hostel
- HR & Payroll
- Inventory & Assets
- Communication & Notifications
- School Administration
- Mobile/PWA
- MIS & Analytics

Phase 18 must integrate with these existing modules.

---

# 1. PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Build a complete:

## Student Lifecycle + Digital Document Vault + Certificate Management + Transfer Certificate System

The system should maintain the student's complete lifecycle from:

Admission

→ Active Student

→ Class/Section Allocation

→ Academic Promotion

→ Reclassification/Section Change

→ Internal Transfer

→ Document Management

→ Certificate Requests

→ Certificate Approval

→ Certificate Generation

→ Transfer/Withdrawal

→ Transfer Certificate / School Leaving Certificate

→ Alumni

while preserving the student's complete historical record.

The system must be suitable for a professional school ERP used by multiple schools.

